  "explanation": {
    "md_es": "**Verbos irregulares:** no llevan -ed; cada uno tiene su propia forma, igual para todas las personas.\n\n| Infinitivo | Pasado | Infinitivo | Pasado |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| go | **went** | buy | **bought** |\n| have | **had** | eat | **ate** |\n| see | **saw** | meet | **met** |\n| do | **did** | come | **came** |\n| get | **got** | write | **wrote** |\n| make | **made** | take | **took** |\n\nHay que memorizarlos poco a poco, en frases: *I went to the market. We ate pizza.*\n\nPronunciación: *bought* /bɔːt/ y *saw* /sɔː/ riman · *ate* /et/ (también se oye /eɪt/).",
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I goed to the cinema.",
        "right": "I went to the cinema.",
        "note": "Los irregulares no llevan -ed."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "We eated pizza.",
        "right": "We ate pizza.",
        "note": "Eat es irregular: ate."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
